# Keep the Docker build context lean and reproducible.
#
# The image builds its own artifacts:
#   - Python deps in the `builder` stage (from requirements.txt)
#   - the frontend SPA in the `frontend` stage (`npm ci && npm run build` -> /fe/dist)
# so host-side build outputs and dependency trees must NOT be copied into the context.

# Node / frontend build inputs & outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Python caches / collected static (regenerated at build/run time)
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
backend/staticfiles

# Orphaned, never-served legacy build output (Django serves the SPA from frontend/dist;
# see backend/config/urls.py). Excluded so `COPY backend` never ships it.
backend/static/assets

# VCS metadata
.git

# Credentials. Secrets reach the container at runtime, as mounts and environment variables,
# and must never be build inputs, wherever someone happens to put them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/cookies.txt
**/cookies*.txt
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*
**/*secret*
!backend/**/*secret*.py

# Durable state and media. `audio` here is only the top-level library folder; backend/audio
# is application code.
/audio
/cache
/data
/es
/redis
/security-reports
/backups
**/celerybeat-schedule*

# Dumps, backups and local databases
**/*.sql
**/*.dump
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.zip

# Local environments and private notes
**/.venv
**/venv
.github
docs
scripts
"build and push.md"
**/*AUDIT*.md
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
